# Design-system compliance audit

This audit applies the completed [design styles](../styles/index.html) and [writing guide](../content/index.html) to the authored design system. It preserves the original findings and records the implemented remedies, current evidence and acceptance checks. Read each resolution alongside its stated test scope.

<% audit = JSON.parse(File.read(File.join(root, 'data', 'design-system-audit.json'))) %>

## Scope and result

<p>The review covers <strong><%= audit['pages'].length %> guidance pages</strong>, <strong><%= audit['examples'].length %> shared examples</strong> and the shared presentation, token and maintained runtime sources listed in the <a href="../reference/design-system-audit.json">machine-readable evidence record</a>. It records <strong><%= audit['findings'].length %> confirmed compliance findings</strong>. “No confirmed finding” means none was identified in the stated static review; it is not a certificate of accessibility or live Home Assistant compatibility.</p>

The [component review](component-audit.html) separately maps every component to its canonical family. The [Home Assistant gap register](missing-components.html) links the completed specifications for the 30 identified design gaps, including functionality already supplied by native Home Assistant. These are different questions from whether existing guidance follows its rules.

The [data, colour, personalisation and illustration review](../reference/data-design-review.json) records the current documentation update and its verification boundaries. It preserves the distinction between a published design reference and implementation inside Home Assistant.

## How the audit was performed

1. Complete the source review and author the brand and writing rules.
2. Review the new rules for conflicts, scope and practical checks. Record their frozen hashes.
3. Read each guide and its examples, then review shared layouts, styles, tokens and maintained runtime boundaries.
4. Confirm each finding against a local rule and a precise source location. Record a proposal and observable acceptance criteria.
5. Reconcile every page and example with the coverage ledger, independently challenge findings, and rerun affected checks.

The [work-package checklist](guidance-work-package.html) records the loops and verification evidence. Source hashes identify what was reviewed. A future edit requires a new review rather than inheriting this result automatically.

## Priorities

| Priority | Meaning | Response |
| --- | --- | --- |
| P1 | Misleading state, action outcome or essential task information | Resolve before relying on that message for the affected household task |
| P2 | Inconsistent presentation, guidance, discoverability or missing required context | Resolve in the next relevant component or documentation change |
| P3 | Maintainability or editorial consistency | Combine with the related content or component revision |

